# Line endings.
#
# Everything in this repository is ultimately executed on Linux — by bash, by helm,
# or by cloud-init on a freshly provisioned VM — even when it is authored on macOS or
# Windows. A Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true (still the default from the Git
# for Windows installer) rewrites files to CRLF, and the results are confusing rather
# than obviously wrong:
#
#   - bash rejects a CRLF script at its shebang: `bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M`
#   - a CRLF .env sets DPL_DOMAIN to "example.com<CR>", which then shows up inside a
#     rendered Ingress host and fails DNS with no visible typo
#   - cloud-init silently skips a user-data file it cannot parse
#
# `* text=auto` normalises to LF inside the repository; the rules below additionally
# pin LF on checkout for the files where CRLF actually breaks something.

* text=auto

*.sh         text eol=lf
justfile     text eol=lf
*.env        text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf
*.yaml       text eol=lf
*.yml        text eol=lf
*.gotmpl     text eol=lf